-- title:
--   Index of speciality of the off-cusp part: ℓ(K-D^∘)+deg D^∘=g
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` for the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ over $K=\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`; divisors are finitely supported $\mathbb Z$-valued functions on the places of $F/K$ in the sense of the project's `Place` structure, and for a divisor $E$ the space `riemannRochSpace` $E$ consists of those $f\in F$ with $v(f)\le \exp(E\,v)$ at every place $v$. Assume $F/K$ carries a canonical divisor in the sense that every nonzero $\omega\in\Omega[F/K]$ admits a divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ordDifferential}\ \omega$, and let $\omega\neq 0$ with `canonicalDivisorOf hω` a choice of such divisor. Let $D$ be a divisor with $D\ge 0$ pointwise, let $D^{\circ}=$ `D.erase (cuspInftyBar N)` be its restriction away from the $q$-adic place at infinity, and assume that `riemannRochSpace` $(D^{\circ}-\overline{\infty})$ is the zero submodule. The conclusion is the equality of integers
--   $$\dim_{K}\ \mathrm{riemannRochSpace}\big(\mathrm{canonicalDivisorOf}\ h\omega - D^{\circ}\big)\ +\ \mathrm{offBaseMass}\ N\ D\ =\ \mathrm{genusFF}\ K\ F,$$
--   where `offBaseMass N D` is the sum of the multiplicities of $D^{\circ}$ and `genusFF` is $\dim_K H^1(0)$.
--
--   This is the index-of-speciality form of the Riemann–Roch theorem for the off-cusp part of a divisor that cannot be lowered at the cusp at infinity: the $\deg D^{\circ}$ conditions imposed by $D^{\circ}$ on the regular differentials are independent, leaving a space of dimension $g-\deg D^{\circ}$ (in particular $\deg D^{\circ}\le g$). It is stated additively so that no truncated subtraction of naturals occurs, and it feeds the positivity estimates for the height pairing on $J_0(N)$, being used by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_baseMass_le_heightForm_of_exists_two_le) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_sum_pairHt_le_of_forall_le_one).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZero_finrank_riemannRochSpace_canonicalDivisorOf_sub_erase_add_offBaseMass.lean

